 "title": "Ledrappier's frozen plane measures distance in signed bits",
 "subject": "What bond distance measures in Ledrappier's law, whose openness all comes from its ends",
 "conclusion": "In Ledrappier's law the three-place knots are exactly the Frobenius triangles, so every point has bond-distance-2 neighbours at every power-of-two separation and every bond ball is infinite. Along each lattice line the bond distance between points n apart is at most 1 + w(n), the weight of n's non-adjacent form, and equals 2 exactly at powers of two.",
